{"chunk_id": "98bf7ddc180d", "text": "This section recounts the death of the great teacher Drona during the Kurukshetra war. After being told that his son Aswatthaman has been slain, Drona loses the will to fight and lays down his weapons. Entering a state of deep yogic meditation, he fixes his mind on the Supreme and spiritually ascends toward heaven, a moment witnessed only by a few great figures including Krishna, Arjuna, and Yudhishthira. Unaware of Drona\u2019s inner transcendence, Dhrishtadyumna fulfills his long\u2011destined vengeance by beheading the defenseless preceptor despite Arjuna\u2019s pleas to capture him alive. Drona\u2019s fall shatters the Kaurava army, causing widespread panic and retreat among its commanders. Aswatthaman, learning of his father\u2019s death, demands the truth. The episode highlights the tragic conflict between dharma, vengeance, deception in war, and spiritual transcendence.\nAfter being deceived about his son\u2019s death, Drona lays down his arms, enters yogic meditation, is beheaded by Dhrishtadyumna, and the Kaurava army collapses in panic.\nThemes: deception in war, death of Drona, yogic liberation, revenge of Dhrishtadyumna, collapse of Kaurava morale", "vector": [-0.009887025691568851, -0.008318508043885231, -0.008016870357096195, -0.0008106523309834301, -0.0036565237678587437, 0.026959741488099098, -0.03061961755156517, -0.014371379278600216, -0.017655882984399796, -0.012755939736962318, 0.012957031838595867, 0.0289840679615736, 0.01038975641131401, 0.016342081129550934, 0.01796422339975834, 0.006042816210538149, 0.03850242495536804, -0.01878199726343155, 0.028206512331962585, -0.031289923936128616, 0.006381321232765913, -0.015551119111478329, -0.003981622867286205, 0.03437333554029465, -0.007473921403288841, 0.01909033954143524, 0.0068639423698186874, -0.029734812676906586, 0.012293427251279354, -0.015658367425203323, -0.012682205997407436, -0.0018869137857109308, -0.004454188980162144, -0.013158123940229416, -0.01045